  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Kiran Rehman, holder of account PK**ABPA****5563, opened on 31 January 2022. The customer's declared occupation is student, with a declared income of PKR 30,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 3 August 2026 to 9 August 2026, the account recorded 15 credits totalling PKR 830,000 as well as 3 debits totalling PKR 784,000. The credits arrived as 15 interbank (IBFT) transfers from 14 distinct senders. The activity was detected on 9 August 2026, when Tazama typology MULE-01 scored 360 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: The account received funds from 14 distinct senders within the activity window. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 94% of credits, with a median of 3.4 hours between the latest credit and each debit. For a customer whose declared occupation is student, credits in the activity window were 27.7 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 30,000 per month. Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected money mule activity; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 472,000 was sent to QuickPay wallet ***0932 (WLT****0932, Synthetic EMI) in 2 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 312,000 was withdrawn as Cash (ATM) in 1 transaction.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 29 August 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (12 August 2026): "Outgoing wallet transfers placed on hold pending review. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
